# Drivetrain Design Evolution

The drivetrain was not fixed from the first prototype.

```text
Early drivetrain
      ↓
Higher-speed configuration
      ↓
High load / stall behaviour
      ↓
Motor and driver failure evidence
      ↓
Re-evaluate gearing and motor
      ↓
600 RPM encoder motor
      ↓
1:1 external gearing
      ↓
Encoder-assisted movement
      ↓
Current Rev27 drivetrain
```

---

## Major Changes

| Area | Earlier Approach | Current Approach | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Motor** | Earlier higher-speed motor | 600 RPM geared encoder motor | Greater operating margin and feedback |
| **External gearing** | 1.5× speed increase | **1:1** | Greater available wheel torque |
| **Movement control** | Mainly timing-based | Encoder-assisted where useful | Better repeatability |
| **Steering protection** | Larger unrestricted corrections | Bounded steering | Reduce linkage stress |
| **Testing** | Full-run diagnosis | Component + integrated testing | Isolate failures faster |

